        desc = "SLCHDRSTRM5 INFERRED, confidence MEDIUM. Reason: the vendor builds a DDR register-config table (table offset 0x34) whose word has the bit layout of the r006 register VEDU_SLCHDRSTRM5, and 9 offsets that the Hi3520D code accesses directly (MODE 0x020, PICFG0 0x024, REGCFG_ADDR 0x1E0, QPTHR 0x350, TARGETBITS 0x364, PICBITS 0x374, MEANQP 0x388, PICINFO0 0xA20, OUTSTD 0x0A4) all sit at the r006 offsets, so the register file is assumed to follow r006 (a neighbor generation). The offset in the window is therefore an assumption, NOT seen in any vendor register access. Register name and field names are the HiSTB drv_venc_reg_r006.h names (naming only). Not accessed by register in any vendor code (it is programmed through the DDR table, loaded by the hardware from REGCFG_ADDR; whether the hardware loads this exact register from the table is the working assumption). SLICE HEADER SOFTWARE BITS, REORDER part word 1. FORMAT RECOVERED 2026-11-11 (docs/rdl-campaign/vedu-vendor.md section 14; board sweep of 40 runs + vendor H264eWrHWSlcHdr 0x50e0): the hardware writes first_mb_in_slice (one bit '1') itself, then ParaWd+1 bits from words 0..3, then (only if ReorderWd != 0) ReorderWd+1 bits from words 4..5, then MarkingWd+1 bits from words 6..7, then slice_qp_delta = se(START_QP - 26) and, with PPS deblocking_filter_control_present_flag = 1, the deblocking syntax (idc, alpha, beta from PICFG0). Each part is packed RIGHT-aligned: MSB-first 32-bit chunks, every full chunk as is, the last chunk shifted to the low bits, so a part of n <= 32 bits is the number in the low n bits of its first word (PROVEN for the PARA part, all 40 runs reproduced bit-exactly; parts above 32 bits and the REORDER part are INFERRED from the vendor packing code only). Example IDR I slice (POC type 2, log2_max_frame_num 4): word 0x20 = 0x000000E1 (ue(2) ue(0) u(4)=0 ue(0)), MARKING word 0x38 = 0 (two zero flag bits), SLCHDRPARA = 0x00400802. Source: docs/rdl-campaign/vedu-vendor.md section 13, H264E_DRV_UpdateRegConfigParam 0x1d4d0 / H264E_DRV_InitRegConfigParam 0x1db40 / H264eDrvUpdateMeCfg 0x1c680. Not verified on hardware.";

        field {
            name = "value";
            desc = "Whole 32-bit word (INFERRED, MEDIUM).";
            sw = rw;
            hw = r;
        } value[31:0];

    } SLCHDRSTRM5 @ 0x074;

