    reg {
        name = "MODLAMBDA16 (INFERRED, MEDIUM)";
        desc = "MODLAMBDA INFERRED, confidence MEDIUM. Reason: the vendor builds a DDR register-config table (table offset 0x2A8) whose word has the bit layout of the r006 register VEDU_MODLAMBDA, and 9 offsets that the Hi3520D code accesses directly (MODE 0x020, PICFG0 0x024, REGCFG_ADDR 0x1E0, QPTHR 0x350, TARGETBITS 0x364, PICBITS 0x374, MEANQP 0x388, PICINFO0 0xA20, OUTSTD 0x0A4) all sit at the r006 offsets, so the register file is assumed to follow r006 (a neighbor generation). The offset in the window is therefore an assumption, NOT seen in any vendor register access. Register name and field names are the HiSTB drv_venc_reg_r006.h names (naming only). Not accessed by register in any vendor code (it is programmed through the DDR table, loaded by the hardware from REGCFG_ADDR; whether the hardware loads this exact register from the table is the working assumption). Index 16 of 20. Vendor default values: see the address map description (40 twelve-bit values, doubling about every 3 steps). Source: docs/rdl-campaign/vedu-vendor.md section 13, H264E_DRV_UpdateRegConfigParam 0x1d4d0 / H264E_DRV_InitRegConfigParam 0x1db40 / H264eDrvUpdateMeCfg 0x1c680. Not verified on hardware.";

        field {
            name = "mod_lambda0";
            desc = "r006 field ModLambda0 (INFERRED, naming and position from the table word, MEDIUM)";
            sw = rw;
            hw = r;
        } mod_lambda0[11:0];

