        desc = "RC1 INFERRED, confidence LOW (a position guess, see below). Register name and field names are the HiSTB drv_venc_reg_r006.h names (naming only). Not accessed by register in any vendor code (it is programmed through the DDR table, loaded by the hardware from REGCFG_ADDR; whether the hardware loads this exact register from the table is the working assumption). POSITION GUESS ONLY: the vendor table words 0x130..0x13C (written once at channel creation: 0x03002100, 0x00050A02, 0x0A0A040F, 0x97888888) are four words that could be an image of QPTHR, RC1, QPDELTATHR0, QPDELTATHR1 (0x350..0x35C). Word 0x134 = 0x00050A02 fits rcQpDelta = 2, rcMadpDelta = 10 (r006 bits [31:16] reserved, value 5 there); the other words do not fit the r006 layouts cleanly. Treat the register, not its fields, as the guess. Source: docs/rdl-campaign/vedu-vendor.md section 13, H264E_DRV_UpdateRegConfigParam 0x1d4d0 / H264E_DRV_InitRegConfigParam 0x1db40 / H264eDrvUpdateMeCfg 0x1c680. Not verified on hardware.";

